    "font" : "Times New Roman",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "56.5 lm W  1 and 26.3%, respectively, with CRI of 86. Even at 10000 and 15000 cd m , high PEs (45.8 and 38.5 lm W  1 ) and EQEs (24.3 and 22.1%) are maintained. Lighting sources are generally characterized by their total emitted light, which is a factor of 1.7-2.3 times more than the forward viewing efficiencies. [1a] Therefore, the present device should have total PE and EQE values approaching 100 lm W –1 and 50%, respectively, at 5000 cd m –2 , which are also the highest levels reported for WOLEDs with extra out-coupling and/or multi-layer tandem structures, [14] as well as comparable to the most efficient lighting technologies. [15]  "
